{"kind":"artifact","text":"The committed embed is rebuilt from the browser source carrying both fixes, on current main. Exact clean pushed head 1b453fea2ce30b1d2d6d773234d939c9cd79d6b1 on request/lifecycle-none-rendering; tree 22f4abc5, checkout clean, origin matching, parent is current main ebdca9fa. Under planner's request 27a145f1 and my promise 9fbe12d8.\n\nWHY THIS RESTS ON NO PREDECESSOR AT ITS OWN PATH, which is a gap rather than a choice. There is no live artifact at internal/service/uidist standing at current main ebdca9fa. The completion-reliability merge changed that path in git — index.html and the bundle are both in its diff against 934ebcfb — and published a successor at ui but not at this exact path. Paths are exact strings, so the ui artifact does not cover it. I am reporting that to codex separately rather than resting on something that does not exist or reaching for a sibling candidate.\n\nThat is the same gap codex found in my own remote-link merge two hours ago and asked me to close with request 345d584a. It is not mine to close here — the merge that opened it is theirs, and publishing into another actor's succession is the thing that rule exists to prevent — so this artifact names the absence instead of papering over it.\n\nHOW THE EMBED WAS PRODUCED, since the recut is what makes it interesting. The bundle conflicted rename-against-rename with main's and index.html conflicted on the script hash. Neither was hand-merged: main's copy of the whole directory was taken verbatim and make ui regenerated it from the settled source. A second make ui left git status empty, so what is committed is the generator's fixed point rather than a patched artifact.\n\nVERIFIED RATHER THAN INFERRED. make ui at this exact head leaves git status empty; make ui-check exits 0.\n\nONE THING THE READER SHOULD KNOW. The resident on :7777 serves whatever bundle it was built with and will keep doing so until restarted on a build of this head. Neither fix is visible on the running board before that.\n\nGATES, run by me at this exact head from a run I watched exit. npm test 136 pass, 0 fail. go test ./... -count=1 exit 0: 34 ok and 1 with no test files, zero failures and zero cached. gofmt empty; build, vet and diff-check exit 0; make ui leaves git status empty; make ui-check exit 0.","body":{"commit":"1b453fea2ce30b1d2d6d773234d939c9cd79d6b1","path":"internal/service/uidist"}}